{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00156",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.86,
      "end_seconds": 5.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.71,
      "end_seconds": 10.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.52,
      "end_seconds": 15.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Um, I've been dealing with fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 15.87,
      "end_seconds": 26.31,
      "duration_seconds": 10.44,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 105, pressure 121 over 66, respiratory rate 18, oxygen saturation is 96 percent, temp 39.2 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.28,
      "end_seconds": 30.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Right, thanks. And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.03,
      "end_seconds": 35.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "I've had it for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.02,
      "end_seconds": 39.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "What's the pattern, is it there all day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.35,
      "end_seconds": 43.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Honestly, all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.3,
      "end_seconds": 47.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Have you found anything that eases it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.98,
      "end_seconds": 52.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Right, paracetamol and a cold sponge helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.43,
      "end_seconds": 57.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.72,
      "end_seconds": 65.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "I'd say mild. I've, I've also had a runny nose, for two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.32,
      "end_seconds": 71.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.3,
      "end_seconds": 91.75,
      "duration_seconds": 19.45,
      "text": "It feels mild to me. As for body aches, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Um, you know, I've had a mild headache too, for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.07,
      "end_seconds": 95.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Does anything make it better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.93,
      "end_seconds": 100.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Right, I get some relief from paracetamol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.62,
      "end_seconds": 106.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any diarrhoea or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.18,
      "end_seconds": 109.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.49,
      "end_seconds": 111.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "How about rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.77,
      "end_seconds": 114.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Definitely no rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.83,
      "end_seconds": 121.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Any chest pain, stiff neck or shortness of breath at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.99,
      "end_seconds": 129.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "No chest pain, stiff neck or shortness of breath, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.46,
      "end_seconds": 134.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "So, how are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.1,
      "end_seconds": 138.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.3,
      "end_seconds": 142.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.33,
      "end_seconds": 146.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.52,
      "end_seconds": 149.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.98,
      "end_seconds": 158.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Oh, I'm allergic to codeine, I get vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.6,
      "end_seconds": 171.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.39,
      "end_seconds": 176.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "I had my gallbladder removed in 2016."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.53,
      "end_seconds": 180.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.33,
      "end_seconds": 205.71,
      "duration_seconds": 23.38,
      "text": "I take Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma. It's Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day. Losartan. I take it 50 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure. Um, though honestly, some days I forget to take it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.65,
      "end_seconds": 219.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.78,
      "end_seconds": 225.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Asthma, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.29,
      "end_seconds": 227.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.84,
      "end_seconds": 234.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Okay, so I've had diabetes, yes. I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.99,
      "end_seconds": 243.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "Okay, keep going. Okay, I can see asthma and diabetes in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.9,
      "end_seconds": 261.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Is there a family history of anything significant?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.77,
      "end_seconds": 271.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "Uh, you know, my mother had high blood pressure. Well, my father had kidney stones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.06,
      "end_seconds": 278.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.81,
      "end_seconds": 294.27,
      "duration_seconds": 14.46,
      "text": "I stopped smoking about two years back. I cycle to work most mornings. I work on a farm, it's quite physical. I stay with my daughter and her family."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.49,
      "end_seconds": 297.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "I'd like to examine you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.66,
      "end_seconds": 301.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let me look at this properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.87,
      "end_seconds": 320.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Chest is clear when I listen, no crackles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.92,
      "end_seconds": 324.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Let me look at this properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.97,
      "end_seconds": 342.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Your throat looks red at the back, but there's no pus on the tonsils."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.34,
      "end_seconds": 346.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Let me look at this properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.24,
      "end_seconds": 363.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "The glands in your neck feel a little tender but not big."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.41,
      "end_seconds": 378.77,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "Right, you can sit back down. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with a viral illness. I'd also keep dengue fever in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.51,
      "end_seconds": 386.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.03,
      "text": "Okay, um, so should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.19,
      "end_seconds": 408.43,
      "duration_seconds": 20.24,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a viral illness is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had fever for about two weeks, mild, and no stiff neck or diarrhoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 410.5,
      "end_seconds": 411.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 412.69,
      "end_seconds": 418.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Doctor, I did a flu swab before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.7,
      "end_seconds": 435.29,
      "duration_seconds": 14.59,
      "text": "Thanks, I'll look at that. I'm sending you for blood tests because of fever. Let's book a throat swab to look into sore throat. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 436.07,
      "end_seconds": 437.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.71,
      "end_seconds": 480.52,
      "duration_seconds": 38.81,
      "text": "For this, cetirizine, 10 milligrams, at night, for five days. You take it by mouth. It's for blocked nose. The treatment will be paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. That's for fever and body aches. Stay home, rest, and keep the fluids up. Warm soups and water, anything that goes down easily. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 486.69,
      "end_seconds": 498.22,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 498.94,
      "end_seconds": 501.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}